# WASM DE2 — two-println join and INT digits only

File: openOODA/audit/wasm_de2.oot
DE2 proof. Re-read wasm_emit_two.oo and wasm_emit_int.oo.
Did not edit either emit file. Did not add runtime if.

Logline: wasm_fn_two_println still joins two STRING texts with one newline, and wasm_fn_println_int still returns INT digits only.
Setup: Token field 0 is kind. Token field 3 is unquoted text from pack_tok. fname is the user function name.
Beats:
  1. After the fname LBRACE, two-println accepts only two println(STRING) statements, optional SEMI each, then RBRACE, and joins the two texts with a newline.
  2. After the fname LBRACE, int-lit accepts only println(INT), optional SEMI, then RBRACE, and returns those digits.
  3. A mixed second print misses. Folded 1+2 misses.

## 0. Unchanged

  two-println unchanged: yes
  int-lit unchanged: yes

  This re-read matches the prior DE2 write-up of both files.
  Public names, match shapes, join, digit return, and residual lines
  are the same. This role did not write those files.

## 1. two-println joins two STRING prints with newline

  ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_two.oo is 88 lines. Under 256.
  Public helper is wasm_fn_two_println.
  Residual line still names three prints and mixed concat as dummy end.
  Grep of this file finds no PLUS, no KW_IF, and no br_if.

  After LBRACE, w2_one_str_println must see:

    IDENT println LPAREN STRING RPAREN

  Optional SEMI only. Then the same shape again. Then RBRACE.
  An INT or IDENT first arg misses. PLUS after STRING is not RPAREN,
  so a strcat chain misses.
  A third println is IDENT, not RBRACE. Three prints miss.

  Hit return is:

    list_get(a, 0) + "\n" + list_get(b, 0)

  That is a compile-time join of the two STRING field-3 texts.
  Not a WASM string heap. Not host strcat. Not a fold of later stmts.

## 2. Two-print fixture

  fixtures/wasm_two_println.oo main body is only:

    println("line-a");
    println("line-b");

  Lexer pack: STRING text is the unquoted body (token_scan_string.oo).
  After main LBRACE the kinds are:

    IDENT println LPAREN STRING line-a RPAREN SEMI
    IDENT println LPAREN STRING line-b RPAREN SEMI RBRACE

  First lit is line-a. Second lit is line-b. Next kind is RBRACE.
  Helper return is line-a, newline, line-b.
  Lock: scripts/wasm_two_println_smoke.oo.

  INT scratch already printed that order under wasmtime:

    line-a
    line-b

  Path: /tmp/grok-goal-3afece913704/implementer/int_two_println.out

## 3. Mixed second print still misses

  After LBRACE the first ident must be println. A leading let misses.
  The second arg must be STRING. An IDENT second arg misses.
  PLUS after that IDENT is not RPAREN. Mixed concat misses.
  After the second optional SEMI the next kind must be RBRACE.

  fixtures/wasm_two_println_hostile.oo main body:

    let x = "x";
    println("keep-me");
    println(x + "no");

  After LBRACE the kind is KW_LET, not println. Two returns "".
  If the first print were the start, the second arg is IDENT x, not
  STRING. Then PLUS, then STRING no. Mixed second print stays dummy.
  Lock: scripts/wasm_two_println_hostile_smoke.oo.

  fixtures/wasm_strcat_mixed.oo is one println of IDENT plus STRING.
  Two wants STRING at the first arg slot. Miss.
  fixtures/wasm_print_hi.oo is one println(STRING) then RBRACE.
  First walk hits. Second walk sees RBRACE, not println. Miss.
  fixtures/wasm_strcat_lit.oo has PLUS after the first STRING. Miss.
  fixtures/hello.oo and wasm_ident_lit.oo start with KW_LET. Miss.

  INT scratch for hostile and mixed: empty stdout. No keep-me-only
  plant. Dummy end holds.

## 4. int-lit still returns INT digits only

  ooda/oodac/wasm_emit_int.oo is 71 lines. Under 256.
  Public helper is wasm_fn_println_int.
  Residual line still names folded 1+2 and non-const ints as dummy end.
  Grep of this file finds no PLUS, no KW_IF, and no br_if.
  FLOAT is named only in the residual beat.

  After LBRACE the next kinds must be:

    IDENT println LPAREN INT RPAREN

  Optional SEMI. Then RBRACE.
  Return is wi_text of that INT token. That text is the digit slice
  from token_scan_number.oo. Not a computed sum. Not a host itoa of
  an add. Digits only.

  fixtures/wasm_int_lit.oo main body is only println(42);
  After LBRACE:

    IDENT println LPAREN INT 42 RPAREN SEMI RBRACE

  Return is 42. Lock: scripts/wasm_int_lit_smoke.oo.
  INT scratch stdout is 42 then newline.

## 5. Folded 1+2 still misses

  println(1+2) token kinds after println LPAREN:

    INT 1  PLUS  +  INT 2  RPAREN

  The helper accepts INT at the arg slot, then requires RPAREN.
  PLUS is not RPAREN. Return is "".
  There is no walk of a second INT. There is no add. There is no
  plant of 3. Folded 1+2 stays dummy end.

  FLOAT is not INT. IDENT is not INT. STRING is not INT.
  Two STRING prints: first arg is STRING, not INT. Miss.
  Hostile two-print: after LBRACE is KW_LET, not println. Miss.
  Extra statements miss. A second println is IDENT, not RBRACE.

## 6. Fold first on main. No runtime if

  ooda/oodac/wasm_emit.oo order on each name:

    hello fold first, and only when name is main
    else print-lit, then ident-let, then strcat, then two-println,
    then int-lit, then const-if

  hello.oo fold is nonempty. main never calls two or int.
  greet is not main. Lit misses. Two misses. Int misses. greet
  keeps dummy end.
  A one-STRING body: lit hits first. Two and int do not run.
  A two-STRING body: lit wants RBRACE after one print. Lit misses.
  Ident wants KW_LET. Strcat wants PLUS in one println. Two then hits.
  A println(INT) body: lit, ident, strcat, and two miss. Int hits.

  fixtures/wasm_if_true.oo after LBRACE is KW_IF, not println.
  Two misses. Int misses.
  fixtures/wasm_if_hostile.oo after LBRACE is KW_LET. Two misses.
  Int misses. This role did not add runtime if. No br_if.

